WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:05.470
It's safe to say that Deadpool 2 has comfortably
avoided sequelitis, with many standout moments

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.390
even surpassing the the first.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:11.929
Nevertheless, this hugely entertaining "family
film" with a twist is not without a few small

00:00:11.929 --> 00:00:12.929
flaws.

00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:16.560
So buckle up and check the weather forecast,
because we're jumping into gale force winds

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.340
to present the five best, and the five worst,
things in Deadpool 2.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.340
Spoilers ahead.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:24.500
Best: A perfect X-Force

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:30.050
First appearing in comic book form in 1991's
New Mutants #100, X-Force's feature film arrival

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:36.340
has been eagerly anticipated since Cable was
first teased in Deadpool's post-credits scene.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:42.120
"But I can tell you one thing and it's a bit of a secret. The sequel? We're gonna have Cable."

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:46.660
Fortunately, their arrival doesn't disappoint,
with Cable, Domino, and Russell fitting into

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:48.110
the team effortlessly.

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:52.960
By the final act, when Deadpool's outfit is
charred in a nod to his grey-suited X-Force

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.719
appearance, it's clear Wade has found his
"F-word."

00:00:55.719 --> 00:00:58.649
Worst: No long-shot action

00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:00.609
Deadpool 2's action definitely isn't bad.

00:01:00.609 --> 00:01:05.550
But fans of director David Leitch's previous
projects, particularly his work on John Wick,

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.110
may feel short-changed.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:09.160
The reason could lie with Leitch's filming
style.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:13.620
Both Keanu Reeves as John Wick and Charlize
Theron in Atomic Blonde performed the majority

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:15.080
of their own stunts.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.350
BUT THAT WASN'T AN OPTION FOR MUCH OF DEADPOOL
2.

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:18.950
Leitch told the Hollywood Reporter:

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:21.720
"You need those actors to want to do it.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:25.060
Otherwise you won't get those genuine characters
on the screen."

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:29.620
Reynolds, however, fractured vertebrae in
his neck on the set of 2012's Safe House,

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:33.020
and, understandably, hasn't performed his
own stunts since.

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:35.180
Best: Domino's luck

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:39.750
As the sole survivor among the new recruits
during the X-Force's inaugural mission, Domino

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:41.460
clearly has what it takes.

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:46.960
In the comics, Domino's superpower is subconscious
telekinesis that kicks in when she's in high-stress

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:47.960
situations.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:51.950
This force field manipulates her surroundings,
and is responsible for jamming the chambers

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:56.060
of guns or manipulating mirrors to blind her
enemies at just the right moment.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:02:00.750
The first time we really see her use those
powers is a beautiful moment in Deadpool 2.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:06.040
Cars somersault and explosions erupt around
her as she nonchalantly escapes harm.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:10.340
Like Final Destination in reverse, she defies
odds in breathtaking fashion.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:13.520
Worst: An under-utilized supporting cast

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:17.520
Most of the first movie's side characters
returned for Deadpool 2, and they were joined

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.170
by a ton of newcomers.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:24.990
The scope is larger, yet Deadpool 2 runs just
11 minutes longer than its 2016 predecessor.

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:28.380
With so many characters vying for screen time,
something had to give.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.810
Morena Baccarin's Vanessa is the most obvious
oversight.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:33.960
Her romance with Wade was integral to Deadpool.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:38.120
In the sequel, Vanessa is shot right at the
beginning, making her little more than Wade's

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:39.710
off-screen motivation.

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:43.910
Reactions to test screenings saw her role
as "wasted," and it's hard to disagree after

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:45.870
watching the final cut.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:48.090
Best: Hilarious cameos

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:51.840
Deadpool's meta humor is primed for scene-stealing
cameos.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:56.620
In the first movie, Stan Lee appeared as a
strip club DJ, and Deadpool wore a printout

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.569
of Hugh Jackman's face as a mask.

00:02:58.569 --> 00:03:00.930
"In case the other fell off."

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:05.170
Deadpool 2 raised the bar with a host of hilarious
appearances from familiar faces.

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:10.100
Old footage of Jackman appears in a callback
to X-Men Origins: Wolverine, but that's nothing

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.810
compared to the rest.

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:15.880
Deadpool's low budget relative to the rest
of the X-Men movies has been a running, self-aware

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:16.880
joke.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:17.880
"I'm gonna wait out here, okay?

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:20.270
It's a big house, funny that I only ever see two
of you.

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:23.480
It's like the studio couldn't afford another
X-Man"

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:28.709
In Deadpool 2, Wade finds himself back at
the X-Mansion after being saved by Colossus.

00:03:28.709 --> 00:03:33.530
As he again rants about the lack of X-Men,
Professor Xavier, Quicksilver, Nightcrawler,

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:37.240
Storm, Cyclops, and Beast appear in a room
behind him.

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:39.870
A Hollywood A-lister makes an appearance,
too.

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:44.900
After colliding with a power cable during
the botched X-Force mission, Vanisher's invisibility

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:49.630
cuts out and the audience can briefly see
his real face, which looks a lot like Brad

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:50.630
Pitt's.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:51.630
Last but not least?

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:56.660
Heavily disguised cameos from Alan Tudyk and
Matt Damon, who appear briefly as a pair of

00:03:56.660 --> 00:04:00.819
friends who get future-tased and have their
truck stolen by Cable after he arrives from

00:04:00.819 --> 00:04:01.819
the future.

00:04:01.819 --> 00:04:03.430
That's an awful lot of hidden star power.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.180
Worst: X-Force Xed out

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:10.900
While Domino, Russell, and Cable were amazing
additions to Deadpool 2, what about the team

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:14.320
members who were introduced only to be brutally
executed?

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:20.350
On their first mission as a team, Bedlam,
Zeitgeist Shatterstar, Vanisher, Domino, and

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:26.380
Peter skydive into high winds, and one by
one, they're all obliterated in gory fashion.

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:30.650
Screenwriter Rhett Reese revealed they deceptively
shot footage to use in trailers to imply the

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:32.750
characters' larger role in the movie.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:37.000
It does make for a funny sequence, but laughter
aside, some viewers couldn't help feeling

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.720
cheated by the quick deaths after that setup.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:44.470
These lesser comic book characters have fans,
their demises were a disappointment for anyone

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:48.500
hoping to see a crew of semi-obscure Marvel
heroes in action.

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:51.270
Best: LGBTQ representation

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:56.972
Deadpool 2 is the first superhero film to
openly include LGBTQ characters in the form

00:04:56.972 --> 00:05:02.100
of Negasonic Teenage Warhead and Yukio, whose
romance is a matter-of-fact subplot throughout

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.100
the film.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:07.710
As for the subtly pansexual Deadpool, his
attraction to Colossus is amped up this time

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:08.710
around.

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:12.690
As well as the occasional metallic fondle
now and again, Deadpool serenades him Say

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:17.090
Anything-style after the pair fall out, and
it's a good thing, too, because Colossus comes

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:20.420
to Wade's aid during the battle against Juggernaut.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.910
Worst: No true supervillain

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:27.030
While the formation of the new super-group
takes center stage in Deadpool 2, the movie

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:28.960
lacks a true big bad guy.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:33.590
The sadistic headmaster of Essex House is
as close as we get to outright villainy.

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:38.430
But it's possible that a certain genetically
altered someone has been lurking in the shadows:

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:39.430
Mister Sinister.

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:44.370
The supervillain made his first full appearance
in The Uncanny X-Men in 1987.

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:49.520
The alter ego of Nathaniel Essex, he shares
a name with Essex House, the orphanage Russell

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:53.680
escapes from, perhaps a tantalizing hint of
Sinister's involvement.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:57.770
He's been teased since a post-credits sequence
of X-Men: Apocalypse, but it's a little frustrating

00:05:57.770 --> 00:05:59.810
that he hasn't appeared yet.

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:01.990
Best: Mid-credits scenes

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:05.780
It wouldn't be a Marvel movie if you didn't
stay glued to your seat during the closing

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:08.449
credits, eagerly awaiting an extra scene.

00:06:08.449 --> 00:06:13.330
This time, Wade outdoes his riff on Ferris
Bueller's Day Off with not one, but three

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:14.720
mid-credits scenes.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:19.180
By the film's conclusion, Cable's time travel
device is used up and he's stuck in the present

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:22.430
after using his final charge to save Wade's
life.

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:27.460
After the credits roll, Negasonic Teenage
Warhead and Yukio fix the device, and, naturally,

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:29.350
Wade quickly uses it to wreak havoc.

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:31.270
First, he travels back to save Vanessa.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:32.360
Easy choice.

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:37.080
Deadpool's next stop is to go back in time
again and save X-Force member Peter, but he's

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:41.890
just getting started, he then makes his way
into 2009's X-Men Origins: Wolverine, where

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:46.530
he makes quick work of his first onscreen
incarnation, shooting the much-maligned mouthless

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:47.530
Deadpool repeatedly.

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:52.290
Then he visits Ryan Reynolds, and shoots him
immediately after he reads the Green Lantern

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:53.290
script.

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:57.300
As Deadpool, Ryan Reynolds used the opportunity
to not only poke fun at himself, but to capture

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:00.180
the kind of "what-ifs" fans love to hypothesize
about.

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:03.520
"I'll tell you who should not have on your
show.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:04.740
Ryan Reynolds.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:07.980
Huge a-hole."

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:10.620
Worst: Missed opportunities

00:07:10.639 --> 00:07:14.699
Not only did the movie lack a clear villain,
but that vacancy could've been filled by at

00:07:14.699 --> 00:07:18.639
least one character who had screen time: Black
Tom Cassidy.

00:07:18.639 --> 00:07:22.830
He amounts to nothing more than a briefly
seen brute, but in the comics, Black Tom has

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:28.060
the ability to channel energy into destructive,
forceful blasts, and a "grander version" of

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:31.080
the character was originally scripted as Deadpool
2's main villain.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:34.669
However, as Rhett Reese told CBR, they reduced
his role, saying:

00:07:34.669 --> 00:07:39.800
"His powers are to move organic material around,
the entire orphanage, and the trees, everything

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:44.900
was flying around, and the hailstorms of wood,
it was really cool, but it was also really,

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:45.740
really expensive."

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:47.340
"Well we don't have that kind of money."

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:51.100
However, there's still hope; Reese confirmed
that Black Tom could return from beyond the

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:52.910
grave at a later date.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:54.139
Thanks for watching!

00:07:54.139 --> 00:07:56.540
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:59.020
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

